<section class="section" id="call-2027" aria-labelledby="call-2027-title">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="card" style="padding: clamp(var(--space-6), 2vw + 1rem, var(--space-8));">
      <div class="featured-eyebrow">Call for applicants · Deadline 7 December 2026</div>
      <h2 id="call-2027-title">2027 edition at the University of Belgrade</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Applications are open for the NetSec Training School at the University of Belgrade, Serbia,
        from 8 to 11 June 2027, alongside the <a href="/2027.html">European Security Studies
        Conference</a> on 10 and 11 June. The deadline is 7 December 2026.
      </p>
      <h3>Who can apply</h3>
      <p>
        Graduate students preparing a PhD proposal, current doctoral candidates, and post-docs within
        one year of their defence, working in security studies broadly conceived.
      </p>
      <h3>What participants get</h3>
      <p>
        Individualised feedback and mentorship from a faculty of senior scholars. Travel costs are
        reimbursed, and participants receive an allowance for the training school and the European
        Security Studies Conference.
      </p>
      <h3>Topics</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>How to research in security studies</li>
        <li>Understanding war, security, strategy, military operations and military organisations from a plurality of approaches</li>
        <li>Methods and fieldwork</li>
        <li>Publishing and the academic career</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>How to apply</h3>
      <p>
        Send a motivation letter, a CV of at most two pages and a 500-word abstract of your research
        proposal to <a href="mailto:ecs.netsec@eiss-europa.com">ecs.netsec@eiss-europa.com</a> by
        7 December 2026. Questions go to the same address.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: var(--space-5); display: flex; gap: var(--space-3); flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center;">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:ecs.netsec@eiss-europa.com?subject=NetSec%20Training%20School%202027%20application">{{ icon("mail") }} Apply by email</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://netsec-cost.eu/summer-school.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ icon("external-link") }} Full details on NetSec</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="card" style="padding: clamp(var(--space-6), 2vw + 1rem, var(--space-8));">
      <div class="featured-eyebrow">About</div>
      <h2>About the Summer School</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        The NetSec Early-Career Scholars Summer School (ECS³) aims to provide training and
        mentorship to Early-Career Researchers (ECR) in order to foster the next generation of
        European security scholars.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is organised jointly by the European Initiative for Security Studies (EISS) and the
        <a href="https://netsec-cost.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">COST Action NetSec</a>, which
        funds it. A partner university hosts each edition: Stockholm University in 2026 and the
        University of Belgrade in 2027.
      </p>
      <p>
        The long-term ambition of the Summer School is to contribute to promoting academic
        excellence in Europe and to nurture the development of a new generation of scholars that
        engage on international &amp; European security issues with their counterparts across the
        globe. It is an excellent opportunity for early career researchers to receive feedback on
        their work, expand their networks, and engage with leading scholars in the field.
      </p>
      <p>
        The inaugural NetSec Summer School took place at Stockholm University from 9 to 11 June
        2026, in the lead-up to the <a href="/2026.html">European Security Studies Conference</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

